/P 168 0 R
/T (### 4. Environmental Contamination Environmental factors can also lead to the contamination of food. This includes the presence of heavy metals and minerals, which can enter the food chain through industrial pollution or criminal adulteration. Additionally, substances from packaging materials can leach into food, further contributing to contamination. Changes that occur during cooking and processing may also affect food safety. Addressing these issues requires stringent environmental regulations and safe packaging practices.)
/E (### 4. Environmental Contamination Environmental factors can also lead to the contamination of food. This includes the presence of heavy metals and minerals, which can enter the food chain through industrial pollution or criminal adulteration. Additionally, substances from packaging materials can leach into food, further contributing to contamination. Changes that occur during cooking and processing may also affect food safety. Addressing these issues requires stringent environmental regulations and safe packaging practices.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
