/T (### 5. Intentional Additives Food manufacturers often add substances to enhance flavor, preserve freshness, or improve nutritional content. Common intentional additives include artificial sweeteners, preservatives, phytochemicals, and modified carbohydrates, especially in functional foods. While these additives can offer benefits, it's essential to ensure that they do not pose health risks. Regulatory bodies often set guidelines and limits for the safe use of these additives in food products.)
/E (### 5. Intentional Additives Food manufacturers often add substances to enhance flavor, preserve freshness, or improve nutritional content. Common intentional additives include artificial sweeteners, preservatives, phytochemicals, and modified carbohydrates, especially in functional foods. While these additives can offer benefits, it's essential to ensure that they do not pose health risks. Regulatory bodies often set guidelines and limits for the safe use of these additives in food products.)
