/T (What is Detoxification? In simple terms, detoxification refers to the process of minimizing or eliminating the toxicity of various chemicals. Fortunately, our bodies have the ability to carry out this function. Through a series of chemical reactions, the body transforms toxic substances into less harmful compounds that can be easily removed. The term 'depuration' signifies cleansing or purifying and can accurately describe how we cleanse our bodies. In reality, the terms detoxification, cleansing, and balancing are often used interchangeably. Balancing refers to achieving internal equilibrium, commonly known as homeostasis, which aids in detoxification, cleanses the body, and promotes restoration of balance. These interactions within our body work together to restore and maintain our health.)
