/Title (Our bodies are constantly undergoing biological changes influenced by internal and external stimuli. Visualizing a well-balanced mobile, where each element interacts, helps to illustrate this concept. Even a slight touch to one component causes movement in others, restoring equilibrium through a new, stable position. Major changes in any element, however, can result in a more complex dynamic shift, often requiring more time to regain balance. While some adjustments to our equilibrium occur quickly, others may take days or even years. If the stress from an imbalance persists, it can hinder recovery. Diseases can arise when bodily functions become rigid, inflexible, and unable to adapt. Resolving such imbalances and identifying their causes can be challenging and time-consuming.)
