/Title (**Insulin**: Active during the absorptive phase to lower blood glucose levels. **Glucagon, Epinephrine, and Cortisol**: These hormones are crucial in the postabsorptive phase to increase blood glucose levels. These hormones coordinate several metabolic pathways to manage glucose anabolism \(building up\) and catabolism \(breaking down\).)
